<title>GERMANY: German insolvencies up 10.2 pct in July yr/yr.</title>
<headline>German insolvencies up 10.2 pct in July yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics</p>
<p>Office reported the following economic indicators:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN INSOLVENCIES     July 96	   Jan-July 96</p>
<p> Total insolvencies		2,808		  18,266</p>
<p> Pct change yr/yr		  +10.2		   +11.4</p>
<p> Company insolvencies	    2,298		  14,797</p>
<p> Pct change yr/yr		  +21.1		   +17.6</p>
<p>W.GERMAN INSOLVENCIES</p>
<p> Total insolvencies		2,013		  13,368</p>
<p> Pct change yr/yr		   +2.0		    +6.5</p>
<p> Company insolvencies	    1,599		  10,489</p>
<p> Pct change yr/yr		  +10.4		   +10.5</p>
<p>E.GERMAN INSOLVENCIES</p>
<p> Total insolvencies		  795		   4,898</p>
<p> Pct change yr/yr		  +38.0		   +27.5</p>
<p> Company insolvencies		699		   4,308</p>
<p> Pct change yr/yr		  +56.0		   +39.6</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
